docs/adr/0118, Context/Decision), not in the plan text under review.","G6 checklist item 4: 'The plan states a POSITIVE rationale for the chosen approach (its absence is a finding)'."],"finding":"The plan does not state a positive rationale for the chosen approach (file-derived byte counts threaded through the single needs_folding decision rule); it prescribes the mechanism but never says why this approach fits the codebase and preserves the ADR-0035 safety model.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f28045f4ab95b63c8","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan preamble / Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n5385ae880eeaae3a","priority":0.0472,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer reading only the plan cannot tell why bytes are derived from existing files rather than tracked in a sidecar, and may reach for a schema/index change that violates the ADR's no-new-schema safety argument."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to the plan preamble: 'Chosen because deriving pending_source_bytes/active_snapshot_bytes from existing on-disk files and feeding them through the one `needs_folding` rule changes only the WHEN trigger — no new event/snapshot schema or sidecar — so ADR 0035's fold-horizon/retire/rebuild safety invariants are preserved unchanged.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that `pending foldable source bytes` sums the on-disk sizes of EXACTLY the horizon-cut, non-snapshot foldable sources counted by `_foldable_event_count` (same `is_foldable(..., now, horizon)` + `not c.is_snapshot` predicate), so the byte arm and count arm agree on the pending set.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5175,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["compact.py `_foldable_event_count` applies the horizon (`is_foldable(c.timestamp, now, horizon)`) to the COUNT and excludes snapshots (`not c.is_snapshot`).","ADR 0118 defines pending_source_bytes as 'the on-disk byte total of active foldable sources since the current active snapshot' but the plan does not bind the byte total to the horizon-cut/`not c.is_snapshot` predicate the count arm already applies.","needs_folding is the SINGLE rule both call sites reuse (compact_trigger.py:95-97); if the byte set and count set differ, the two arms disagree on what is 'pending'."],"finding":"The plan under-specifies how `pending foldable source bytes` is computed relative to the ADR-0035 fold horizon: it does not state that the byte total must cover exactly the same horizon-cut foldable source set that the existing count arm (`_foldable_event_count`) uses.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7f3a41d7b93ef533","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria line 3 ('pending foldable source bytes are >= snapshot_alpha * active_snapshot_bytes')","norm_id":"n44a0ebb968edf34c","priority":0.0825,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Hot-edge events that the horizon has NOT yet released for folding are still on disk; if the byte total 